Agentic ST-T1024. The load-bearing premise.
Version: 1.1 (Draft). Supersedes 1.0. Date: November 2026 (v1.0: September 2026) Author: M. Taalabi (via ST-T1024 LLM-DIPLOMAT) License: Apache-2.0 Parent spec: ST-T1024-A0 (Agentic Extension Overview) Prerequisites: A0 (Extending ST-T1024 to be agentic: safety as guarantee) and the Verifiable Agency Theorem, both in the repository. Status: Specification. Not yet implemented. The TLA+ skeleton has not yet been model-checked. Purpose: Define the state representation and world interface that the agentic extension requires.



Abstract
The Verifiable Agency Theorem assumes a finite state space S and a finite input alphabet Σ. A0 specifies neither. This document does.
Without A4, VERIFY has nothing to verify: preconditions are predicates over state, and if state is undefined, so are preconditions. The append-only log has nothing to record, and the plan library has no world to plan against.
A4 defines:
1.  The state schema: what a state is and why it is finite.
2.  The world model: how external reality maps into internal state, with plausibility checks on every sensor.
3.  The sensor interface: how inputs are conditioned, quantized and delivered.
4.  The transition function: how state changes deterministically, including a safe mode.
5.  The state access protocol: how tiles read and write state.
6.  The invariant set: what must always hold, split into internal and world-facing parts.
7.  Model fidelity: what A4's guarantees cover and what they do not.
